{
  "about": "The paper and the frame on the back of a postcard. Yours to edit. A paper is a CSS background (colors, gradients, patterns), so no picture files are needed. Write {c0} to {c4} anywhere in a background to use that day's five palette colors; add two letters after it for see-through, so {c1}40 is that color at 25 percent. grain is how rough the paper feels, 0 to 1. lines: false hides the ruled lines (for dotted or graph paper). Keep papers light enough for dark handwriting. A frame is either a band (width px of a CSS background, drawn around the edge, inset px in from it) or a line (a CSS border, inset px in, radius px for rounded corners). The first paper and the first frame are what a new postcard starts with. The order here is the order in the tray.",
